Upstream bug: wildcard deployments lose native streaming capability
metadata.

https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/21090
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/37800
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/37801

Adapted metadata propagation, not a direct backport: an explicit deployment
model_info.supports_native_streaming decides whether a streamed Responses call
is faked, without requiring base_model or exact graph entries. Deployments
that leave it unset keep the upstream provider decision.

Removal check: tests/verify_streaming.py

diff --git a/litellm/responses/main.py b/litellm/responses/main.py
--- a/litellm/responses/main.py
+++ b/litellm/responses/main.py
@@ -1387,6 +1387,12 @@
         if custom_llm_provider is None:
             raise ValueError("custom_llm_provider is required but passed as None")

+        # A wildcard deployment's resolved model may be missing from the model cost
+        # map, which reads as "no native streaming"; its explicit model_info decides.
+        native_streaming: Final = (
+            deployment_model_info.get("supports_native_streaming") if isinstance(deployment_model_info, dict) else None
+        )
+
         response = base_llm_http_handler.response_api_handler(
             model=model,
             input=input,
@@ -1400,8 +1406,12 @@
             timeout=timeout or request_timeout,
             _is_async=_is_async,
             client=kwargs.get("client"),
-            fake_stream=responses_api_provider_config.should_fake_stream(
-                model=model, stream=stream, custom_llm_provider=custom_llm_provider
+            fake_stream=(
+                not native_streaming
+                if stream is True and isinstance(native_streaming, bool)
+                else responses_api_provider_config.should_fake_stream(
+                    model=model, stream=stream, custom_llm_provider=custom_llm_provider
+                )
             ),
             litellm_metadata=kwargs.get("litellm_metadata", {}),
             shared_session=kwargs.get("shared_session"),
